WEBVTT

00:58.250 --> 01:00.040
That one seems rather peculiar.

01:00.670 --> 01:03.460
I'm sensing a somewhat unfathomable
power behind him.

01:03.460 --> 01:05.420
So, you've noticed?

01:05.420 --> 01:08.040
That man is actually favored to be
the champion of this tournament.

01:08.250 --> 01:09.880
His name is Helck.

01:10.380 --> 01:13.790
He battled his way through the
preliminary rounds with outstanding results.

01:14.000 --> 01:16.210
He's a hero from the human realm.

01:16.830 --> 01:18.670
Did you just say human hero?!

02:49.880 --> 02:54.790
<b>Helck the Hero</b>

03:07.460 --> 03:09.210
Off in a distant land,

03:09.210 --> 03:13.080
there was a lone hero who managed
to defeat the powerful Demon Lord.

03:13.500 --> 03:22.750
<b>Castle Thor</b>

03:14.170 --> 03:15.380
Seizing the opportunity,

03:15.380 --> 03:19.250
the human army stormed the
Demon Lord's castle and took control of it.

03:19.250 --> 03:22.080
This marked their victory over
the Demon Lord and his forces.

03:22.920 --> 03:25.460
Shouts of joy and celebration
flooded the human realm,

03:25.460 --> 03:29.170
as all fear they had of the Demon Lord
was washed away.

03:32.040 --> 03:34.920
Then, roughly three months passed.

03:34.920 --> 03:38.710
And here in the Demon Realm,
a fierce competition was getting underway

03:38.710 --> 03:42.040
to fill the empty throne
left behind by the Demon Lord.

03:44.080 --> 03:45.790
I am Vermilio.

03:46.250 --> 03:51.210
<b>Combat Level: 78</b>

03:46.250 --> 03:51.210
<b>Four Elite Lords of the Empire:</b>

03:46.250 --> 03:51.210
<b>Vermilio the Red</b>

03:47.040 --> 03:48.710
Since Azudra is out with an injury,

03:48.710 --> 03:51.210
I will serve as manager
for the tournament in his place.

03:51.210 --> 03:54.210
My name is Hon and I serve
as submanager for the tournament.

03:51.210 --> 03:54.170
<b>Administrative Level: 48</b>

03:51.210 --> 03:54.170
<b>Tournament Submanager: Hon</b>

03:54.210 --> 03:55.830
Nice to be working with you.

03:55.830 --> 03:58.540
Getting right to business,
how is the tournament proceeding?

03:58.540 --> 04:01.670
We just finished with the preliminary rounds
as of yesterday.

04:01.670 --> 04:04.040
There are many skilled warriors participating,

04:04.040 --> 04:06.960
so hopes are high that we shall bear witness
to the rise of a new Demon Lord

04:06.960 --> 04:08.960
who surpasses even that of the late Lord Thor.

04:08.960 --> 04:11.630
And our security?
I assume the barrier is holding up well?

04:11.630 --> 04:14.580
Everything has been upgraded and
reinforced since the last tournament.

04:14.920 --> 04:19.500
Furthermore, to ensure that all participants
can engage in pure competition

04:19.500 --> 04:23.130
we've prepared this little document
known as the "Deep Green Contract."

04:23.130 --> 04:24.000
I see.

04:24.000 --> 04:25.830
Azudra working his magic, as usual.

04:25.830 --> 04:27.460
Indeed.

04:27.460 --> 04:28.380
Wonderful.

04:28.380 --> 04:31.250
Then moving on, I would like to see
some of the preliminaries firsthand.

04:31.250 --> 04:32.420
Did you record any of it?

04:32.420 --> 04:33.250
Yes.

04:33.250 --> 04:34.830
I have it all right here.

04:41.170 --> 04:43.380
Hmm. How interesting.

04:43.790 --> 04:47.210
The average level of the combatants
for this tournament is 45.

04:47.210 --> 04:49.750
That's a record high for us.

04:51.460 --> 04:54.420
With warriors of that caliber,
we can do better than just take back our realm,

04:54.420 --> 04:58.170
we may even be able to claim some of the land
owned by those foolish humans!

04:59.540 --> 05:01.330
That one seems rather peculiar.

05:01.580 --> 05:04.080
I'm sensing a somewhat unfathomable
power behind him.

05:04.790 --> 05:06.710
So, you've noticed?

05:06.710 --> 05:09.000
That man is actually favored to be
the champion of this tournament.

05:09.250 --> 05:10.790
His name is Helck.

05:10.790 --> 05:13.670
He battled his way through the
preliminary rounds with outstanding results.

05:13.670 --> 05:15.830
He's a hero from the human realm.

05:16.210 --> 05:17.210
Oh?

05:18.040 --> 05:20.080
DID YOU JUST SAY HUMAN HERO?!

05:20.080 --> 05:22.080
What the hell is a human doing here?!

05:22.080 --> 05:22.920
Huh?!

05:22.920 --> 05:24.920
Because he managed to survive
the preliminaries, ma'am...

05:24.920 --> 05:26.790
But why is he even participating?!

05:26.790 --> 05:29.330
Well, anyone is allowed to participate
in the tournament regardless of race...

05:29.330 --> 05:30.960
EXCEPT FOR HUMANS, OBVIOUSLY!

05:30.960 --> 05:32.830
What?! Why can't they participate?!

05:32.830 --> 05:34.290
They're our mortal enemies!

05:34.290 --> 05:35.460
Mortal enemy?

05:36.500 --> 05:38.000
Oh please, have no fear!

05:38.000 --> 05:39.750
He may be a human, but his end goal is-

05:39.750 --> 05:40.710
WHAT?!

05:41.880 --> 05:44.250
W-well, please just take a look at this...

05:44.250 --> 05:46.130
That was such an incredible victory!

05:46.130 --> 05:48.750
Please share a few words
about how you're feeling right now!

05:49.500 --> 05:51.380
I despise humans!

05:53.920 --> 05:56.130
Let's destroy them all!

06:01.830 --> 06:04.290
And so, there's nothing to worry about.

06:04.290 --> 06:06.250
YOU FOOL!

06:06.250 --> 06:08.330
HE'S OBVIOUSLY JUST FAKING IT!

06:08.330 --> 06:10.080
HE HAS LIAR WRITTEN ALL OVER HIS FACE!

06:10.080 --> 06:11.380
Please calm down, ma'am...

06:11.380 --> 06:13.500
A human hero has invaded our sanctuary!

06:13.500 --> 06:15.040
Why did you leave him be?!

06:15.040 --> 06:17.080
Didn't anybody stop to consider
the consequences?!

06:17.080 --> 06:18.630
Do you all just want to die?!

06:18.630 --> 06:20.790
Uh, gosh, well, I'm sure it'll be fine...

06:20.790 --> 06:22.580
EXACTLY WHAT PART OF THIS IS FINE?!

06:22.580 --> 06:25.080
I mean, he signed the Deep Green Contract.

06:26.630 --> 06:31.040
The power of this document nullifies all attacks
that are made against people outside of the ring.

06:31.040 --> 06:34.290
So the participants are literally incapable
of hurting anyone.

06:34.540 --> 06:36.330
Even the great hero Helck

06:36.330 --> 06:39.420
doesn't have enough strength
to overcome the force of the contract.

06:39.420 --> 06:40.330
All right, then.

06:40.330 --> 06:43.040
So you're telling me
this hero is essentially powerless?

06:43.040 --> 06:44.000
Exactly.

06:44.000 --> 06:47.380
There is no being alive who can escape
the binding contents of the contract

06:47.380 --> 06:49.580
until the tournament has come to an end.

06:49.580 --> 06:52.080
No... I simply can't believe this.

06:53.750 --> 06:55.540
And Chupabra goes down!

06:55.540 --> 06:56.630
The contest...

06:57.460 --> 06:59.960
Wait! I know what he's after!

06:59.960 --> 07:03.040
That's a count of 10!
Helck is now officially the victor!

07:03.170 --> 07:03.920
Oh my!

07:03.920 --> 07:08.380
It seems Helck is slowly approaching
Chupabra instead of leaving the ring!

07:08.580 --> 07:11.380
He's using the contents
of the contract to his advantage!

07:11.380 --> 07:15.250
Because right now, nobody but his opponents
in the tournament can stand against him!

07:15.580 --> 07:17.920
Chupabra is still down for the count!

07:17.920 --> 07:20.960
What exactly does Helck intend to do here?!

07:20.960 --> 07:22.790
And just like that,

07:23.040 --> 07:26.580
he'll fight through the tournament
matches while slowly but surely

07:26.580 --> 07:30.290
slaughtering every warrior we have
with the potential of becoming Demon Lord!

07:30.290 --> 07:32.420
Look at that! He's reached out a hand!

07:33.290 --> 07:34.750
That was a wonderful fight!

07:35.210 --> 07:36.830
You trounced me.

07:36.830 --> 07:39.210
Now this is a touching scene!

07:39.210 --> 07:41.040
Seems like that's not the case at all.

07:41.040 --> 07:43.210
THEN WHAT THE HELL DOES HE WANT?!

07:43.210 --> 07:46.670
W-well, is it so hard to believe that he's legitimately
interested in becoming Demon Lord?

07:46.670 --> 07:47.920
THAT'S RIDICULOUS!

07:48.080 --> 07:50.880
He obviously has some kind
of ulterior motive here!

07:50.880 --> 07:53.040
Besides, even if he did win the tournament,

07:53.040 --> 07:55.670
there's no way the citizens
would just accept him as Demon Lord!

07:56.080 --> 07:57.170
You rock, hero!

07:57.170 --> 07:58.000
We love you!

07:58.000 --> 07:59.580
Kick ass, man!

08:00.420 --> 08:02.130
Seems like that won't be a problem...

08:02.420 --> 08:04.040
FOOLS!

08:05.500 --> 08:07.460
Doesn't anybody around here
have a sense for danger?!

08:07.750 --> 08:09.170
I mean, come on!

08:09.170 --> 08:11.210
We're practically begging
the humans to invade us!

08:11.210 --> 08:12.670
Please compose yourself...

08:12.670 --> 08:13.500
Yeowch!

08:13.500 --> 08:16.380
We're out of options.
I'll just have to eliminate the human myself!

08:16.710 --> 08:18.540
Uh, so about that contract I mentioned earlier...

08:18.540 --> 08:21.330
it also nullifies any attacks
that we make upon the participants.

08:21.330 --> 08:22.830
HOW STUPID CAN YOU GET?!

08:23.040 --> 08:26.080
Then hurry and make him fight
someone who can beat a hero!

08:26.080 --> 08:30.500
Um, the only problem with that
is Helck has a combat level of 99...

08:31.790 --> 08:34.000
Level 99, are you freaking serious?!

08:34.210 --> 08:36.380
The hero is gonna win for sure, dammit!

08:36.380 --> 08:38.960
Which is why I said he's the one favored to win...

08:38.960 --> 08:41.420
THEN WE'RE ALL DOOMED, YOU MORON!

08:50.130 --> 08:52.920
Ah, it's been a while
since we've had such a clear sky.

08:53.420 --> 08:57.540
How the hell does any human reach level 99
with their short lifespans?

08:57.960 --> 09:00.880
Curses! We're in deep trouble now!

09:00.880 --> 09:01.960
If I may...

09:01.960 --> 09:05.580
will I be facing any sort of punishment
for this incident?

09:05.790 --> 09:07.290
Of course you will.

09:07.290 --> 09:09.830
And let me tell you that
a simple demotion won't cut it.

09:09.830 --> 09:12.750
Wah! Oh, please no! I don't want to die!

09:12.750 --> 09:14.880
I'm the one who should be crying right now...

09:14.880 --> 09:16.960
Th-then let's come up with a good strategy!

09:16.960 --> 09:20.540
Do you honestly think there's any way
for us to beat a level 99 hero?!

09:21.040 --> 09:23.290
Oh! I've got an idea!

09:23.290 --> 09:24.290
That was fast.

09:25.000 --> 09:27.380
We can just change the format
of the next tournament match...

09:28.000 --> 09:30.380
I'm going to be absolutely livid
if you suggest something like poker!

09:31.380 --> 09:32.330
Yipes!

09:32.330 --> 09:35.330
No, um, my idea was actually to build a house!

09:35.330 --> 09:36.250
A house?

09:36.250 --> 09:38.170
Yes! A house of cards!

09:38.170 --> 09:41.210
Whoever is the first to build one
will be declared the winner!

09:41.210 --> 09:45.920
And on top of that, I'll make sure the hero
gets provided with these extra glossy cards...

09:46.130 --> 09:50.000
Well, I'll admit that would definitely
help level the playing field for us.

09:50.000 --> 09:53.170
But we're talking about a tournament
that decides the next Demon Lord!

09:53.170 --> 09:54.960
Think of how the citizens
and participants would react!

09:54.960 --> 09:57.920
Please, ma'am! Just give me a chance!

09:57.920 --> 09:59.210
Hmm, I'm not sure...

09:59.210 --> 10:00.880
Please! I'm begging you!
Hmm, I'm not sure...<b></b>

10:00.880 --> 10:01.710
Please! I'm begging you!

10:07.330 --> 10:09.880
This is the human realm.

10:10.920 --> 10:13.790
<b>Spy Level: 55</b>

10:10.920 --> 10:13.790
<b>Intelligence Operative: Asta</b>

10:10.920 --> 10:13.790
<b>(Works for Vermilio)</b>

10:11.040 --> 10:13.830
And this is Asta, a demonkin spy.

10:13.830 --> 10:16.380
Under the orders of Vermilio,

10:16.380 --> 10:20.580
she was dispatched with the objective of
gathering information about the hero Helck,

10:20.580 --> 10:22.790
and was about to start her mission.

10:22.790 --> 10:23.830
However...

10:24.000 --> 10:26.420
There's not a soul around here.

10:27.000 --> 10:28.540
What should I do?

10:31.830 --> 10:33.170
Hello?

10:41.920 --> 10:43.040
Well, that's that.

10:43.040 --> 10:46.210
I'll just have to report back with
the info I have regarding the current situation.

10:53.500 --> 10:57.750
I was really concerned about how everyone would
react to this silly "house of cards" idea, but...

10:58.250 --> 11:00.080
Here come our warriors!

11:02.920 --> 11:05.250
So they're doing something different
than a battle this time?

11:05.250 --> 11:06.790
It's a whole mew ballgame now!

11:06.790 --> 11:09.040
...they welcomed it without a second thought!

11:09.040 --> 11:11.830
We appreciate your patience, everyone!

11:12.250 --> 11:14.500
It's time for the playoffs
to decide a new Demon Lord!

11:15.210 --> 11:17.080
Here we go!

11:28.540 --> 11:29.750
Pretty dull, huh?

11:29.750 --> 11:31.380
That's an understatement.

11:31.380 --> 11:33.580
The rules of this match are extremely simple!

11:33.580 --> 11:36.380
All the participants have to do
is complete a 10 story house of cards!

11:41.250 --> 11:45.290
Only those who rank in the top 10 will be able
to make it to the next round of competition!

11:45.290 --> 11:48.290
Who among these warriors
will be the first to finish?!

11:48.920 --> 11:50.420
Oh my! Helck is struggling!

11:50.420 --> 11:52.380
Perhaps he's not very good at stacking cards?

11:52.380 --> 11:55.670
He seems to be falling pretty far behind
compared to the other participants!

11:58.080 --> 12:01.040
Just look at Helck!
He's struggling like a fish out of water!

12:01.040 --> 12:03.540
He hasn't even managed
to complete the bottom floor yet!

12:03.710 --> 12:06.460
That said, I feel sorry for the warriors
who will fail here

12:06.460 --> 12:09.210
without getting the chance
to show their full potential.

12:09.630 --> 12:10.670
No matter.

12:10.670 --> 12:13.420
We can just put any of the
noteworthy ones under my command.

12:13.420 --> 12:14.830
Send me the list of registered fighters later-

12:24.710 --> 12:26.170
I must hone my focus.

12:51.420 --> 12:52.710
S-such speed!

12:52.710 --> 12:55.790
Helck is moving like a blur
as he quickly stacks layer upon layer of cards!

13:00.630 --> 13:02.170
H-he's finished!

13:02.170 --> 13:04.920
Helck has completed his house of cards!

13:06.670 --> 13:07.880
That's just ridiculous!

13:07.880 --> 13:10.750
How the hell does someone move that fast
without knocking the cards over?!

13:10.750 --> 13:12.750
Hey! Isn't that against the rules?!

13:12.750 --> 13:14.000
Woof! Woof, woof, woof!

13:14.000 --> 13:15.670
Yeah! He broke the rules!

13:15.670 --> 13:17.920
I never imagined
there would be interference like this.

13:17.920 --> 13:20.710
But I'm not sure it's a good idea
to try and tack on new rules now...

13:20.710 --> 13:21.920
It's fine!

13:21.920 --> 13:23.630
This is obvious enough to go without saying!

13:23.630 --> 13:24.920
Against the rules?

13:24.920 --> 13:26.790
Now that's just silly talk.

13:26.790 --> 13:28.130
What did you say?!

13:28.420 --> 13:31.000
Come on, did you seriously
think this was nothing more

13:28.460 --> 13:33.080
<b>Combat Level: 38</b>

13:28.460 --> 13:33.080
<b>Kenros the Godspeed</b>

13:31.000 --> 13:33.130
than a race to build a house of cards?

13:33.130 --> 13:34.000
Huh?

13:34.130 --> 13:35.040
Huh?

13:35.290 --> 13:36.830
Let me break it down for you.

13:37.130 --> 13:39.540
The house of cards that we're building
is meant to represent our home base.

13:39.920 --> 13:41.710
In other words, the Demon Lord's Castle!

13:41.710 --> 13:46.040
The action of stacking cards together is synonymous
with expanding the castle to greater heights!

13:46.040 --> 13:50.580
So, in essence, this is a contest where we must
protect our castle while wiping out our opponent's

13:50.580 --> 13:52.250
by juggling both offense and defense!

13:52.540 --> 13:54.500
That gust of wind triggered by his aura

13:54.500 --> 13:58.250
was something we all should have defended
against by using whatever means necessary!

13:58.790 --> 14:01.790
Because anyone incapable
of even finishing this simple castle of cards

14:01.790 --> 14:03.750
has no right to become the Demon Lord!

14:03.960 --> 14:06.000
Got it? You've had your chance!

14:06.000 --> 14:07.790
Why is he reading so much into this?!

14:07.790 --> 14:09.170
That's way off base!

14:09.330 --> 14:11.380
Who's the idiot peddling all that crap?

14:09.500 --> 14:13.130
<b>Combat Level: 50</b>

14:09.500 --> 14:13.130
<b>Hyura the Immortal</b>

14:11.380 --> 14:13.170
There's no way that's right.

14:13.170 --> 14:15.750
Wowee! This house of card stuff is deep!

14:15.750 --> 14:18.000
Hot damn, I totally knew there
was something more to this match!

14:18.000 --> 14:19.000
Now I get it!

14:20.330 --> 14:24.540
Okay, with that settled,
it seems Helck is the first to finish!

14:26.920 --> 14:28.540
Shit! I ain't out yet!

14:28.540 --> 14:29.250
Whoa! Watch it!

14:30.460 --> 14:31.670
Hey, don't burn the cards!

14:31.670 --> 14:32.580
Take this!

14:36.880 --> 14:39.920
Well, it's impossible to make interference
against the rules now...

14:39.920 --> 14:40.880
Dammit.

14:41.130 --> 14:43.170
That meathead was
confident from the get-go.

14:43.170 --> 14:45.380
He already knew he could win this!

14:45.380 --> 14:48.460
So he intentionally pulled that stunt
to throw the entire match into chaos,

14:48.460 --> 14:50.630
and turned everyone else
against each other in the process!

14:50.630 --> 14:53.040
Now the majority of participants
are going to end up getting injured!

14:53.040 --> 14:54.580
That was his plan all along!

14:54.580 --> 14:56.500
P-please calm down, ma'am!

14:56.500 --> 14:58.540
It's never good to
read so deeply into things...

14:58.540 --> 14:59.670
This was just an accident.

15:00.630 --> 15:03.250
How the hell are you so chill right now?!

15:03.500 --> 15:05.210
FOOL!

15:06.130 --> 15:07.420
Whoa! Are those fireworks?!

15:07.420 --> 15:08.670
They must be!

15:08.670 --> 15:10.130
Far out!

15:12.250 --> 15:13.210
Asta?

15:16.710 --> 15:21.630
<b>Spy Level: 48</b>

15:16.710 --> 15:21.630
<b>Intelligence Operative: Ista</b>

15:16.920 --> 15:18.580
Took you long enough to report in.

15:19.290 --> 15:21.080
Sorry, Ista.

15:21.670 --> 15:24.080
Type 2 Special Abilities.

15:24.420 --> 15:26.630
Some citizens of the empire
have these special abilities

15:26.630 --> 15:29.420
that can be activated upon
fulfilling certain conditions.

15:30.040 --> 15:36.080
For example, the twins Asta and Ista are capable
of sending messages between each other

15:36.080 --> 15:38.290
through the action of drinking coffee.

15:38.540 --> 15:40.330
Okay, so what's the situation like?

15:40.330 --> 15:42.790
Well, I figured a lot of stuff out.

15:43.170 --> 15:45.500
But first, I'm most interested in hearing
how the tournament's going.

15:46.380 --> 15:47.960
Checkmate.

15:47.960 --> 15:49.210
You've bested me.

15:50.040 --> 15:52.330
Helck claims yet another victory!

15:52.330 --> 15:55.790
This is exactly why you should've moved
that damn pawn, fool!

15:55.790 --> 15:57.790
W-we'll get him in the next one for sure!

15:57.790 --> 15:59.210
It's going to be a sculpting match,

15:59.210 --> 16:02.250
and I made sure his carving knife
is duller than a rusty axe!

16:02.540 --> 16:03.710
I'm finished!

16:05.630 --> 16:07.880
And there you have it,
10s across the board!

16:07.880 --> 16:09.460
The cooking showdown is coming up next

16:09.460 --> 16:11.880
and I'm going to make sure
he gets stuck with a child-sized apron...

16:11.880 --> 16:13.880
Just put me on the panel of judges!

16:13.880 --> 16:16.000
I'll give whatever dish he cooks a big fat zero!

16:16.000 --> 16:18.250
What?! You're going
to show yourself in public?!

16:18.250 --> 16:19.500
Don't have a fit.

16:19.500 --> 16:23.000
I'll wear a disguise so that everyone thinks
I'm nothing more than an ordinary judge.

16:39.540 --> 16:40.630
Tasty...

16:42.420 --> 16:45.580
Helck has done it!
He's on his way to the semi-finals!

16:45.580 --> 16:47.540
Please tell us how you're feeling!

16:48.000 --> 16:50.000
The demon realm is so fun!

16:53.500 --> 16:55.210
I wasn't able to lie...

16:55.500 --> 16:57.420
God, I'm such a fool!

16:57.420 --> 17:00.290
Argh! I knew I should've
served a dessert instead!

17:00.580 --> 17:03.460
That judge...
She seems familiar somehow...

17:03.460 --> 17:05.630
Dammit! His food was tasty!

17:05.630 --> 17:06.960
And I mean SUPER tasty!

17:06.960 --> 17:10.920
Um, please keep a lid on your temper because
an explosion here would lead to casualties...

17:10.920 --> 17:12.330
I know that!

17:14.960 --> 17:16.630
What the hell is with this poster?!

17:16.630 --> 17:18.380
I haven't seen any of these guys out there!

17:18.380 --> 17:19.540
What are they, mere models?!

17:19.540 --> 17:21.130
O-oh no, far from it!

17:21.130 --> 17:24.500
They were all highly skilled fighters
expected to win the tournament!

17:24.670 --> 17:27.420
Up until Helck took them out
in the preliminaries, that is...

17:27.420 --> 17:28.670
WRARGH!

17:28.830 --> 17:30.170
Oh, this is bad!

17:30.170 --> 17:31.830
She's gonna blow her top!

17:31.830 --> 17:32.880
I must raise a barrier!

17:35.750 --> 17:37.710
Uh, what the...

17:38.040 --> 17:39.380
Do you have any tape?

17:39.380 --> 17:41.170
Um, yes.

17:47.880 --> 17:49.580
Things can't continue like this.

17:49.580 --> 17:51.790
I must find a way to protect our citizens!

17:52.630 --> 17:53.710
Lady Vermilio.

17:55.250 --> 17:57.790
I've just gotten some information
on Helck from Asta.

18:00.500 --> 18:02.710
Yo, Helck! Great job out there!

18:02.960 --> 18:04.210
Why hello, Kenros!

18:04.460 --> 18:06.960
Whatcha looking at there?
Some kinda paper?

18:06.960 --> 18:09.130
It's a picture. Would you like to see?

18:09.130 --> 18:10.330
Can I really?!

18:10.330 --> 18:11.540
Nope!

18:11.920 --> 18:13.080
You jokester!

18:13.080 --> 18:14.170
Lemme see!

18:16.170 --> 18:17.250
Come on now!

18:18.250 --> 18:20.630
The crap peddler and that infernal hero.

18:20.630 --> 18:23.790
Just look at them making
all that obnoxious racket over there.

18:24.210 --> 18:27.540
I wouldn't want to touch either of them
with a 10-foot pole.

18:27.540 --> 18:30.670
Helck the hero actually has
an enormous bounty on his head.

18:30.670 --> 18:33.830
And he's been labeled as the worst criminal
in all of human history.

18:34.750 --> 18:36.250
The crime he committed...

18:36.670 --> 18:38.080
was fratricide.

18:39.210 --> 18:40.170
Hmph.

18:40.170 --> 18:42.960
Even heroes are still
just human in the end, huh?

18:42.960 --> 18:44.790
Such a moronic race.

18:45.210 --> 18:47.790
So, what can you tell me
about the brother he killed?

18:47.790 --> 18:49.960
Yes, about that...

18:50.830 --> 18:53.790
His brother was the hero
who brought down Demon Lord Thor.

18:54.960 --> 18:55.830
What?!

18:55.830 --> 18:58.250
Then Helck isn't the one
who defeated the Demon Lord?!

18:58.250 --> 18:59.290
Correct.

18:59.290 --> 19:01.040
That hero was named Cless.

19:01.040 --> 19:04.540
It seems there were two heroes
born into the world this time.

19:04.540 --> 19:06.210
Yoink! It's mine now!

19:06.210 --> 19:08.540
Aw, shucks. Feel free to look, then.

19:09.000 --> 19:10.830
Oh, is this guy your brother?

19:10.830 --> 19:12.790
Yep. That's right.

19:13.040 --> 19:15.630
Gosh, you two look totally... not the same.

19:15.630 --> 19:17.750
He's way more of a dreamboat then you are!

19:17.750 --> 19:19.040
I know, right?

19:19.040 --> 19:20.540
He gets it from our mother!

19:20.750 --> 19:22.500
A dreamboat, you say?

19:22.500 --> 19:24.540
There's one more odd thing I should mention...

19:24.960 --> 19:27.710
Asta said that she visited three different towns.

19:28.000 --> 19:31.040
But she couldn't find
a single human in any of them.

19:31.040 --> 19:32.080
What?!

19:32.500 --> 19:33.830
Based on how things were left,

19:33.830 --> 19:37.790
it seems like people had been
living there like normal until very recently.

19:41.420 --> 19:43.380
Lady Vermilio! Trouble at one of the castles!

19:43.380 --> 19:46.380
I'm afraid to report
that Castle Urum has just fallen!

19:46.540 --> 19:47.710
That's impossible!

19:47.710 --> 19:50.630
Demon Lord Urum should have a combat level
of 60 up there with the other elites!

19:51.080 --> 19:54.170
Where the hell did the humans find warriors
with enough strength to compete against that?!

19:54.170 --> 19:56.580
Are you telling me they have
even MORE heroes?!

19:56.580 --> 19:57.630
Even more?

19:57.630 --> 20:00.750
N-no, it wasn't a hero.
They were some kind of strange knights.

20:01.040 --> 20:03.040
White knights that had wings.

20:03.330 --> 20:06.960
Apparently, their strength was far beyond
any of the previous human warriors we've fought.

20:06.960 --> 20:10.170
But as far as I know,
there's no such thing as winged humans.

20:10.170 --> 20:11.830
Are the citizens okay?!

20:11.830 --> 20:13.330
Put your mind at ease.

20:13.330 --> 20:16.420
The Demon Lord stepped up and
sacrificed himself to buy everyone some time,

20:16.420 --> 20:20.750
which allowed for most all of the soldiers
and citizens to escape safely.

20:21.290 --> 20:22.580
Oh, wow...

20:23.420 --> 20:25.500
He must have fought hard.

20:25.500 --> 20:26.920
What incredible bravery.

20:31.290 --> 20:32.630
Rock, paper, scissors!

20:34.880 --> 20:35.880
I hate to say it,

20:35.880 --> 20:39.290
but is there any chance the humans have
caught on to the existence of the capital?

20:39.540 --> 20:42.040
It's not really concerning
if they've figured out that much.

20:42.500 --> 20:45.960
The biggest issue right now is the undeniable fact
they've marched upon this decaying land

20:45.960 --> 20:48.290
and captured Castle Urum.

20:48.290 --> 20:51.380
Because if they still have strength left to fight,
the next place they'll come for is here!

20:51.380 --> 20:54.250
Reinforce the barrier and prepare
our forces for combat immediately!

20:54.540 --> 20:55.540
Understood.

21:03.210 --> 21:05.790
I didn't feel a thing from that attack
thanks to the power of the contract!

21:05.790 --> 21:06.630
Crazy, huh?

21:10.920 --> 21:12.210
Those human bastards!

21:12.880 --> 21:15.000
What diabolical means have they used now?!

22:45.920 --> 22:50.710
<b>Next Episode</b>

22:45.920 --> 22:50.710
<b>Anne from Management</b>

22:46.750 --> 22:49.880
Next time: "Anne from Management"
